{"body":"Accept as verified partial progress: **unsolved, 5/5**. The five results establish a finite-degree exact search under effective-coordinate and strict numerical hypotheses; weighted auxiliary-line certificates; modular arrangements with controlled additions; Fermat deletion criteria; and a specific infinite subfamily with an exact Seshadri constant. The general complex line-arrangement conjecture remains unresolved.\n\nRoot and distinct adversarial families checked all five universal arguments and executable sources. A fresh source-first whole-package reviewer passed headde6889b0ca34ceba9a08b85637272afe0b14af77. Full replay reproduces214070 author and93918 historical assertions. All47 Git bindings,46 unchanged mathematical files, historical chains,72 final evidence files and11 initial seal instances verify. Root also reproduced the fresh baseline/extension programs and exact final-head gate. Detailed incidence records agree under a uniquely checked permutation of the three unordered coordinate vertices; summary outputs are byte-exact.\n\nThe auxiliary-cover audit strengthens only the specific subfamily: optimum4q forq>=2 and11/3 forq1, while its Seshadri value stays1/(4q+1). This is a checked audit deduction, not a sixth author turn, novelty claim or general solution. Public wrappers verify0 optional source files; separate fresh PDF checks and the unreproduced historical PNG are recorded explicitly.\n\n[Acceptance decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr378_30004322/ACCEPTANCE_DECISION.md) · [fresh adversarial review](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_descending_audit_20261002/audits/pr378_30004322/clean_final_adversary/audit_report.md).\n\nAI tools were used extensively in research, drafting, verification and adversarial review. The work is unrefereed and has not received external human peer review. Accept the scoped partial outcome; no paper, Zenodo deposit, DOI, tracker row or release.\n","headRefOid":"de6889b0ca34ceba9a08b85637272afe0b14af77","isDraft":false,"mergeCommit":{"oid":"4600b719b1a8c58498acb35d82a52267e52285d8"},"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":"2026-10-03T06:36:05Z","state":"MERGED","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/378"}
